        "original_id": "f8a6fb24-8dde-561d-b69f-7f54f1705f78",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elia Kazan, William Inge, David Amram, Zohra Lampert, Natalie Wood, Warren Beatty\n- Products: Splendor in the Grass, Let's Scare Jessica to Death\n- Topics: film, acting, directing, screenwriting\n\nFacts:\n- Elia Kazan was born as Elias Kazantzoglou on September 7, 1909, and he died on September 28, 2003.\n- Elia Kazan was a Greek-American director, producer, writer, and actor.\n- The New York Times described Elia Kazan as one of the most honored and influential directors in Broadway and Hollywood history.\n- Zohra Lampert was born on May 13, 1937.\n- Splendor in the Grass is a 1961 Technicolor drama film about a teenage girl dealing with sexual repression, love, and heartbreak.\n- Splendor in the Grass was written by William Inge, who won an Academy Award for the screenplay and appeared briefly in the film as a Protestant clergyman.\n- Splendor in the Grass was directed by Elia Kazan and features a score by jazz composer David Amram.\n- Zohra Lampert starred alongside Natalie Wood and Warren Beatty in Splendor in the Grass.\n- Zohra Lampert played the title character in the 1971 cult horror film Let's Scare Jessica to Death.\n- Zohra Lampert is an American actress with roles in film, television, and stage.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
